<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lankan blue chips fall on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Sri Lankan blue chips fall on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of three highly capitalised blue chips fell on profit-taking in early Friday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>Shares of Hayleys Ltd fell 2.2 percent or five rupees to 220, John Keells Holdings Ltd 2.1 percent or five rupees to 230 and Development Finance Corporation of Ceylon Ltd 1.4 percent or 3.75 to 270.</p>
<p>&quot;These scrips are easing on profit-taking after rising sharply on thin volumes in the recent rally,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Colombo stocks, which gained over 15 percent in four weeks due to improved investor sentiment, began correcting on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
